<blockquote class="uncited"><div>While this might seem on the face of it to be a good idea, I have one reservation - this forum seems to be more than adequately supplied with users who don't bother reading sticky posts (eg., how to install OpenGD77) as it is, and my concern is that those same users would fail to read the sticky and assume from the mere presence of the topic that the developers are, in fact, working development of a CPS variant for Linux.<br><br>I seem to recall (open to correction here) that the developers have in the past rejected the idea of topic areas not directly related to OpenGD77 for a similar reason.</div></blockquote>Good and valid point.<br><br>Since I posted, I did find the post I was thinking of in the General Discussions. It just took manual digging and searching to find it. My frustration comes from the search function not being able to help me find that thread.<br><br>Roger and those that directly help him have done fantastic work over the years in developing / supporting  the GD77 firmware. For myself, when it comes to 2m and 70cm usage, I do not want to even consider a radio that does not operate with the GD77 firmware. I just wish there was some way those of us that are or will be Linux based can coordinate efforts and experience to support GD77 on Linux.<br><br>I am open to any and all suggestions, just hoping we can find one that is practical and manageable for all involved.<br><br>AA3RP<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1814">AA3RP</a> — Thu Feb 27, 2025 5:55 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
