While this might seem on the face of it to be a good idea, I have one reservation - this forum seems to be more than adequately supplied with users who don't bother reading sticky posts (eg., how to install OpenGD77) as it is, and my concern is that those same users would fail to read the sticky and assume from the mere presence of the topic that the developers are, in fact, working development of a CPS variant for Linux.<br><br>I seem to recall (open to correction here) that the developers have in the past rejected the idea of topic areas not directly related to OpenGD77 for a similar reason.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4176">ZL2MGS</a> — Wed Feb 26, 2025 10:51 pm</p><hr />
